  "note": "rank-39 (5,24) has no fresh row and no single-sharer row: both rows arrive with exactly two prior sharers (row 5 via index 2 = the rank-3 root (5,19) and index 25 = the rank-26 root (5,16); row 24 via index 4 = the rank-5 root (18,24) and index 14 = the rank-15 root (15,24)), and both double in the triple, quad and quint layers for the first time (54/391/763 and 46/259/179 records). The new pair census is 4 shared / 34 disjoint -- the fewest shared of the whole post-fresh-row era -- and the new-layer double-row family gains two rows in one generation (rows 5 and 24 join; the quint histogram now spans 17 rows 0, 1, 4, 5, 7, 8, 9, 11, 14, 15, 16, 18, 19, 23, 24, 29, 30). STRUCTURAL BREAK AT k=39: the new quint layer contains 508 disjoint records (all with 10-row unions), the first disjoint quints ever (every published k=26..k=38 quint census had disjoint == 0, which is what let the k=38 marginal I-E carry only the b_only term j5_B at level 5), and the C(39,6)=3,262,623 sextet census contains 5,852 b_only records (double rows confined to the hub band rows 15/18/19, every record containing the rank-39 root), the first non-zero sextet layer ever (the C(38,6) census was all zero). Both premises of the k=38-style truncation therefore fail at k=39: the main computation must evaluate the level-5 disjoint-quint joints (j5_A, alternating level-5 sign) and the level-6 b_only-sextet joints (j6_B, alternating level-6 sign) before truncating. Level 7 closes the hierarchy: every C(39,7)=15,380,937 7-combo with a non-zero 6-subset was scanned (99,122 distinct candidates via the upward closure of the zero class, since disjoint sextets do not exist at k=39) and all are zero, so the I-E truncation at level 6 is well-defined. The 157 -> 1,009 jump in new disjoint quads (all 8-row unions, cumulative 2,686 = 1,677 + 1,009 confirmed by a global C(39,4) recount) is the same lightly-shared-root effect as the 508 disjoint quints.",
  "ie_extension": {
   "level5_disjoint_quints": "508 records, the first ever; their class no longer forces zero joints, so the k=38-style identity m - sum_j2 + sum_j3 - sum_j4 + sum_j5B no longer holds as stated: the disjoint-quint joints (j5_A) must be evaluated with the alternating level-5 sign",
   "level6_b_only_sextets": "5,852 records, the first ever (all contain the rank-39 root); their B-type joints (j6_B) must be evaluated with the alternating level-6 sign",
   "level7_and_beyond": "all zero (99,122-candidate monotone extension scan), so the marginal I-E truncates at level 6 once the two new terms are included"
  },
